# Phase 2+ frontend lifecycle

Applies to **Phase 2 through the final phase**. Skip this lifecycle only for pure backend/infra with no UI. This setup task must not implement Phase 2.

Load skill `caratom-phase-frontend` and follow it. Summary:

## Before writing code

- Read relevant `Vibe code principles/` files and the current phase spec.
- Review Expo / Vercel RN / frontend-design skills that apply.
- Inspect existing components and tokens; reuse before creating new ones.
- Note mobile UX, accessibility, and performance risks.

## During implementation

- Follow product authority (see `caratom-design-authority` rule).
- Follow native mobile UX and the relevant Expo and React Native skills.
- Prefer reusable components; keep visual consistency; no unnecessary libraries.

## After implementation (mandatory)

Do **not** declare the phase complete after coding. Audit the **entire application**, not only new files, against vibe-code principles, mobile UX, visual quality, design-system consistency, accessibility, performance, and edge states (loading/empty/error/disabled/success/partial/long text/small+large screens/keyboard/network).

Fix in-scope findings, then re-audit. A later phase that exposes a Phase 2 inconsistency should flag and fix it when appropriate so the app gets more consistent over time.

Use the completion checklist in `caratom-phase-frontend`. Only then mark the phase complete.
